map.[roe] - bod zlomu.event.6.descriptio:
{Sunny - creator of Breaking Point}

You have successfully completed
{the first part of the game}, in which you had to capture the castle called Golden City. I know it probably was not easy, but you can be proud of yourself. It really was no simple task. May your good fortune continue ...

map.[roe] - bod zlomu.event.7.descriptio:
{Narrator}

{The Griffin Lord}, a noble magnate, leader of all living griffins on the Elurian frontier and lord of Angel Grove, is surprised that someone called Kosmix is paying him to wear red colours and banners and defend his castle against enemies for as long as possible. He has never seen an enemy in his life.
But {what if???}

map.[roe] - bod zlomu.guards.0.0.1.messa:
{THE BREAKING POINT HAS COME!}
{YOU HAVE OBTAINED THE ARTIFACT FOR ME!}
{LONG LIVE KOSMIX, MASTER OF THE WORLD, HEH HEH HEH!}

Why is Kosmix laughing?
And where is your newly acquired prize vanishing before your eyes?

Why, now that the game is over,
do you feel that the die has only just been cast?

{Congratulations, you are a true hero. Like SUNNY!}

map.[roe] - bod zlomu.guards.0.57.1.mess:
'He killed ten of the titan’s children for no reason, and then the titan himself!'
'Really?!'
'Yes, Father ...'
'Very well, ruler of all mages. I shall visit righteous punishment upon him!'

Whose voices were those?
Were they talking about you?
And what punishment?

{At least your third question}
{received a clear answer.}
{The punishment has just flown in!}

map.[roe] - bod zlomu.guards.0.62.1.mess:
{'Grandioso, my pupil'}

Are you imagining it, or is that truly the voice of your master Kosmix?

{'Mighty spells have carried you far}
{from Alexandr’s company so that you,}
{like all the others, may fulfil your}
{part of the task ...'}

What task? Master ... Master Kosmix?!

map.[roe] - bod zlomu.guards.0.63.1.mess:
{'I know nothing of your task except}
{that you will need all your}
{magical abilities, so I wish}
{to help you with a little mana and power ...}
{But I truly know nothing}
{of your task. Someone mysterious has begun}
{a game for high stakes and ...'}

The master fell silent. What is this about? What is happening now???

map.[roe] - bod zlomu.guards.0.67.1.mess:
At last!

{Another message from your master:}

'Among the elementals below, in the region called Hubnik, you can learn spells and the schools of their respective elements. Choose carefully which elements to visit first, because you can advance to a higher level in 
{no more than two schools of magic!}

{And do not squander your strength!'}

map.[roe] - bod zlomu.guards.0.70.1.mess:
'If you wish to learn Air Magic, then learn it you shall! Along with the proper spells ...' the wind whispered in your ears.
Then it swirled and howled around you for a long time ... 

{Something is happening to you!}

map.[roe] - bod zlomu.guards.1.69.1.mess:
{'Grandioso!'}

Ah. Kosmix again.

'I tried to influence several dozen crusaders passing through this dead forest so that they would be willing to join you. I hope it worked. And one more important thing. Namely ... er ... that ...'

{'Kosmix!'}
{'KOSMIX!!!'}

map.[roe] - bod zlomu.guards.10.70.1.mes:
'Oh dear, this forest looks rather vast. And I still have no idea where I am going, or what I am after,' you sigh rather grandiosely. How else?

What awaits you behind the next tree?

{Whither goest thou?}

map.[roe] - bod zlomu.guards.12.69.1.mes:
{'Where the devil himself shakes?}
{Hah hah hah! Someone here}
{has clearly lost his wits to fear ...'}

Smoke appears out of nowhere before you. When it clears, horror strikes: the devil himself, here in this forest! He seems to be shaking with eagerness for battle rather than fear! 
{'Damn!'} you exclaim.

{Too late for curses!}

map.[roe] - bod zlomu.guards.2.59.1.mess:
Kosmix speaks again, but his voice is broken and unsteady, trembling or shaking, almost rattling ...

{'Your mana is ... do not go ... vengeance ...}
{quickly ... tent ... soon ... I, I, nooo!'}

{KOSMIX! WHAT IS HAPPENING?}
Something must have happened to Kosmix! This is bad ...

map.[roe] - bod zlomu.guards.2.70.1.mess:
'If you wish to learn Fire Magic, then learn it you shall! Along with the proper spells ...' crackles an enormous scarlet flame, towering beside you.
Then it coils around you, but you feel neither pain nor heat, only ... 

{something strange happening to you!}

map.[roe] - bod zlomu.guards.21.22.1.mes:
{ALEX, I HOPE YOU ARE TRULY STRONG!}
{FOR EVEN THE DARK LORD}
{STANDS AGAINST YOU!}
{HE HAS JUST SENT}
{SOME OF HIS MONSTERS AT YOU!}
{STAND FIRM AND FIGHT!}
{SAVE US!}
{GET THAT MAGIC CAPE!}
{YOU ARE SO CLOSE!}
{FIGHT!}

Thus spoke Kosmix ...

And a moment later they attacked! Drunken monsters!

map.[roe] - bod zlomu.guards.26.50.0.mes:
'Alexandr!' a voice thunders, or perhaps a hundred voices?
'Surely you do not think we will simply let you leave after desecrating our sacred field of inscriptions! Only a hundred pegasi a year can be silvered here, and you squander this place’s energy for an entire year! You shall be punished!!!'

{They take flight! They attack!}

map.[roe] - bod zlomu.guards.28.25.1.mes:
An extraordinary, unknown, unearthly force hurls you to the ground. It is as though brutally strong hands seize you, grip you tightly, and then something approaches your head. 
Rather like your beloved drawing near. But this is no pleasure. Quite the opposite: it is bad, very bad. Your strength is rapidly leaving you!

{Has the BREAKING POINT come?}

map.[roe] - bod zlomu.guards.29.26.1.mes:
'Breaking Point? What point, for heaven’s sake? Kosmix, what did all that mean? I have thousands of questions ...'

A brilliant flash cuts short your speech. The sky darkens, and suddenly you know that something, somewhere, is about to break. Perhaps inside you?

{To go or not to go? That is the question.}
{Would it be wiser to turn back...?}

map.[roe] - bod zlomu.guards.3.60.1.mess:
'Come and play with us, sir. It will be such tremendous fun,' says a strange {eye}. An eye with little legs, looking fairly harmless. But appearances can deceive, and you have grown used to many strange things in this forest.

Nothing for it: you prepare your men to confront the eyes.
{There seem to be rather a lot of them!}

map.[roe] - bod zlomu.guards.3.63.1.mess:
You ponder what the mages said about turning Kosmix’s spell against you. How? You hope it will not be disastrous. Yet even Kosmix himself sounded worried last time. What will happen?

The clash of weapons breaks your reverie. You see crowds of crusaders. More men for your army!
{Or ... perhaps not?}

map.[roe] - bod zlomu.guards.3.65.1.mess:
{'Grandioso!'}
{'Why did you help yourself in this way?'}
{'Why???'}

'Kosmix?! Kosmix!!!'

No, Kosmix speaks no more. What happened? What have you done? Where did it go wrong???

map.[roe] - bod zlomu.guards.30.27.1.mes:
{'ALEX!'}

That is KOSMIX! Why is he calling now? How does he mean to help, or what does he want?

{'Alex, you still have a DOZEN steps to the BREAKING POINT!}
{Proceed only if you are strong enough,}
{for otherwise only death awaits you!}
{May Strength, Spells and Wisdom guide you...'}
{Break a leg, lad...'}

map.[roe] - bod zlomu.guards.30.38.0.mes:
Perhaps now you will finally learn why there is so much sulfur here! As you picked up the last pinch, you felt someone’s hot breath. You wondered briefly where it came from, and then there was suddenly nothing left to wonder about.

{Why was there nothing left to wonder about?}
{Because he was already flying towards you!}

map.[roe] - bod zlomu.guards.33.31.1.mes:
{Sunny - creator of Breaking Point}

In just a moment it will come. {The Breaking Point!}
Perhaps you are ready to enter the final part of the game! But is your Alexandr truly strong and wise enough to pass?

What of tomorrow? Who can tell?
Tomorrow they lie in coffins as well!

map.[roe] - bod zlomu.guards.38.27.0.mes:
'So YOU no longer want to live? You no longer like this woooorld of God’s? Then you are just the man for me, or half a man, looking down at you from up here. Your sort is my speciality! How about giving me your soul???'

You search for words, then find them:
{'I would sooner tear off your ears!'}

map.[roe] - bod zlomu.guards.39.23.0.mes:
'We warned you!' comes a voice from the right.
'And we want to help you!' comes another from the left.

It seems several dozen flies want to join you, while roughly as many leave you, form groups with the others, and look distinctly aggressive.

{There will be a fight, oh yes!}
{Strike, strike, strike ... the flies upon the head!}

map.[roe] - bod zlomu.guards.4.1.1.messa:
'The way ahead is blocked, which means ... I need wings!'

{Or at least a little Red Bull!}
{Though another flying spell would be welcome too!}

Why must this Obelisk and these mountains stand right here, when I can plainly sense that the cape is so close?

map.[roe] - bod zlomu.guards.4.57.1.mess:
'The law has FLOWN in with us!' cries one of the seven black dragons ambushing you.
You have no particular reason to welcome this draconic performance. But since they have flown in, {they will not fly out!}
{At least, not on their own wings!}

map.[roe] - bod zlomu.guards.40.24.0.mes:
'More flies are joining you, eh, dear little Liliputek? But they do not know what we know!' one of your old flies mouths off at you, rather foully. 'You cannot talk your way out with verse this time. One more step and I mutiny. 
{And I will not be alone!!!}'

{A splendid day, eh, Liliputek?}

map.[roe] - bod zlomu.guards.48.66.0.mes:
'The Cursed Island, then. Lucky me again. Not a living soul anywhere. Only dead souls. Damn it. I want to be with Alex. I would even welcome Adriana, who thinks Alex belongs to her alone. If only Alex would give me a sign that he is thinking of me!'

{Something magical happens!}

{ 'Oh, Alex!'}

map.[roe] - bod zlomu.guards.49.31.0.mes:
{Liliput! Liliput!}

(it sounds like Alex again: does he know telepathy or something?)

{Hurry! Please!}
{I have so little time to spare!}
{And knowing you, my friend, I fear}
{you and your horse can barely crawl,}
{mourning Jasmína’s death through it all!}
{BUT I NEED YOU! HURRY!}

map.[roe] - bod zlomu.guards.52.15.0.mes:
'Some strange beasts are climbing aboard! We will not let them on, will we?' shouts a crewman.
They look beastly indeed. You will have to kill them, for they do not look remotely peaceful.

{At them, then!}

map.[roe] - bod zlomu.guards.54.51.1.mes:
'So this is the magic Head that mage spoke of!' you blurt in surprise. 'Let us hope I can get it from those ugly harpies flitting around it!
{Its effect could be,}
{well, overwhelming!}'

map.[roe] - bod zlomu.guards.55.3.0.mess:
'I told you, I told you, I told you!' cries the wounded zealot, looking ready to gather up his feet and robes and flee at the first opportunity.
You try to display your charisma, boldly facing those among the rocks.

{'Well, surely you do not want a fight?'}
{'You do not stand a chance, you old farts ...'}

map.[roe] - bod zlomu.guards.58.8.0.mess:
Sniffer claims his place in the sun:
{'I would sail six miles}
{to the southeast!'}
he reports, looking as though he has swallowed all the wisdom in the world.

map.[roe] - bod zlomu.guards.6.70.1.mess:
'If you wish to learn Water Magic, then learn it you shall! Along with the proper spells ...' 
comes a voice from deep beneath the earth. Then a terrible downpour streams straight onto you, while your entire company stays dry.

{Something very strange must be happening!}

map.[roe] - bod zlomu.guards.61.1.0.mess:
'Thank you, Adrianka, for defeating that rotten scoundrel,' comes the familiar voice of the forest’s Spirit from somewhere to the right.
'I still wish to repay you for the hatchet,' he continues. 'Perhaps one of my spells will help a little ...'

{You feel energy spreading through your body,}
{ you feel stronger and mightier...}

map.[roe] - bod zlomu.guards.61.69.0.mes:
The first cloud arrives before you can even look around properly, accompanied by Lord Ironik’s familiar, ironic voice.
'Here I am again, with the honour of welcoming you, my friend. I bring word that this little trick, on my honour, will cost you your life, and I shall laugh? Ready to be afraid? 
{You have every reason!}

map.[roe] - bod zlomu.guards.64.14.0.mes:
Sniffer claims his place in the sun again:
{'I would sail five miles} 
{to the north-north!,'}
he reports, looking as though he has swallowed all the wisdom in the world.

map.[roe] - bod zlomu.guards.64.3.0.mess:
Again wind whispers through the crowns of still taller trees. You long to flee home. Their trunks move, their branches lean towards you, 
and you can only grin cynically: 
{'What, seeking revenge for your little brothers?}
{Leave me alone. I have no nappies with me.'}

Something runs down your thighs. Probably sweat.

map.[roe] - bod zlomu.guards.64.9.0.mess:
Sniffer speaks up again, now looking positively like a superman.
{'I would look somewhere near that log ...,'}
{'Something smells odd here, though ...,'} he adds.

map.[roe] - bod zlomu.guards.65.2.0.mess:
Wind whispers in the crowns of tall, stately trees. Their trunks move, their branches lean towards you, and you see anger, terror, madness and fury in eyes that seem ready to burn you to ash.

Quietly, you sigh: 
{'Things look bad for me again ...'}

map.[roe] - bod zlomu.guards.65.4.0.mess:
Tangled roots block your weary horse’s progress until an ulcer troubles your belly. Sadly, that is not the worst of it: just as the pain peaks, another delightful group of trees attacks.
You want to tell them to get lost in the woods...
{but they are already in the woods.}

map.[roe] - bod zlomu.guards.68.4.0.mess:
'Surely you did not think you had escaped, accursed monster, arrogant murderer of our children, you ...' rumble voices from the treetops at the edge of this damned forest.

After all your battles with trees, you feel quite entitled to reply: 
{'As the forest calls, so shall I fell it ...'}

map.[roe] - bod zlomu.guards.70.4.0.mess:
'Surely you did not think you had escaped, accursed monster, arrogant murderer of our children, you ...' rumble voices from the treetops at the edge of this damned forest.

After all your battles with trees, you feel quite entitled to reply: 
{'As the forest calls, so shall I fell it ...'}

map.[roe] - bod zlomu.guards.70.6.0.mess:
'Ah, at last I'm out of that stupid forest,' Adriana sighed blissfully as a wonderful feeling of freedom spread through her body. She could breathe the lovely fresh, moisture-laden air ... 
'Good heavens, surely that isn't the sea?!' little Adriana cursed.
{'I can't swim ...'}

map.[roe] - bod zlomu.monster.0.27.1.mes:
'We are {Kosmix's First and Highest Mage!}
Kosmix's most devoted servants.
I am to tell you, Lord Alexandr, that Breaking Point will come. Soon {Breaking} {Point!} will be upon us. Do you understand?! 
And now we shall help you one last time, so that you may reach Breaking Point!'

{Kosmix's Mages treacherously attacked you!}

map.[roe] - bod zlomu.monster.12.2.0.mes:
'Where the hell is that hydra reunion after a hundred and eleven years? Why is everything such Chaos? And who the hell are you now? I'm sick of someone or something always pissing me off here! Clear?!'

'Yes, perfectly clear, Mrs Hydra, I ...'

{Further words seem quite pointless ...}

map.[roe] - bod zlomu.monster.13.7.0.mes:
'Hey, you there. So there's no hydra reunion here, is there? And why were you laughing earlier? And why are your people's weapons stained with hydra blood?'

'Their what - cheeks unshaven for a whole week? I can't hear you properly, hydra!' you try to save the situation again. 'Hydra!'

{'Did someone say Otter?' the hydra exclaims triumphantly.}

map.[roe] - bod zlomu.monster.14.4.0.mes:
'We're going to the hydra reunion. Are you organising it???'

'Me? No, why? I'm just passing through.'

'Then where did you and your people make those hydras who already passed this way disappear to?'

Oh, damn. How do you get out of this ... 'Which hydras, if I may ask?'

{Apparently you may not, because once}
{again nobody is listening to you.}

map.[roe] - bod zlomu.monster.19.25.1.me:
'Can't you see we're arguing over which princess each of us gets? Can't you see we're having a very, very important meeting that takes place once every hundred years? Can't you see!!! And you'll never see anything again! Hey, whoever kills him gets Princess Arabela!'

Trouble again. But this time it's
{big, black trouble!}

map.[roe] - bod zlomu.monster.35.31.0.me:
Dozens of strange creatures climbed out of the mire.
They piously beat their shins with their flails.
They look as though this world God made 
Will bring you and your companions only trials.

{So what shall we do with them?}
{The order to attack has already been given!}

map.[roe] - bod zlomu.monster.4.54.0.mes:
'Welcome! We are the guardians of unfulfilled wishes. Anyone whose wish the genies could not grant may come to us, and we shall help. We know what troubles you, so now we wish to help you!'

'But I don't want that anymore, I wanted ...'

{Unfortunately, "help" is already on its way!}

map.[roe] - bod zlomu.monster.41.41.0.me:
'Welcome, vile trespasser! We welcome you, vile, vertically overdeveloped viceroy of all the earthbound vliliputs, vanguard of viciously vexing dragon flies. We shall vanquish you ...'

{You were getting sick of that volley of Vs!}
{'Now I'll claim a V of my own!' you cried.}
{'V for Victory!'} You waved your hand and ...

map.[roe] - bod zlomu.monster.47.28.0.me:
'Shrimp!' cried the hydra in many voices.

You looked all around to see whom they meant.

'We mean you, you little runt! There's nobody else that small here, is there!?' they continued.

{But that made you angry.}
{They shouldn't have called you that.}
{What a nasty provocation!}
{They'll be mincemeat for that!}

map.[roe] - bod zlomu.monster.55.61.0.me:
'Well, well, the bloodless ones are wandering about here. We can't even drink from them,' calls one of the flying maniacs, whose teeth are particularly well developed.
'And they want to get past us. Suuuurrrre they do!' jeers another, whose fangs are as long and sharp as sabres.

{If only you could turn them into bats for good ...}

map.[roe] - bod zlomu.monster.55.70.0.me:
'A cloud here, a cloud there, what shall I do to whom, and where?' recites a lich with revolting hair, rather clumsily. He hasn't noticed you yet, but ...

{Unfortunately, now he has.}
And he is already firing. A nasty cloud full of deadly stench and general unpleasantness. Lately that stench seems to be everywhere ...

map.[roe] - bod zlomu.monster.56.69.0.me:
'Well, what have the devils dragged in? What do you want here, heroine? Better return ... with our help ... to your grave. Come, meet your death, come!' says one of the mighty liches who have just attacked you.
How will you deal with these fellows? That is the question.
{ To beat or not to beat them?}

map.[roe] - bod zlomu.town.58.45.1.event:
Welcome to your new Golden City, Augustus!

Would it help if I built a town building with your gold and a few other resources? I hope so. Good luck ...

{Your Kosmix}

map.[roe] - bod zlomu.town.71.43.0.event:
{Angel Grove}

Some villagers from below the castle saw the dreaded Lord of Lightning nearby. 
Since they enjoy life under your rule, they helped you repair the ruined Heavenly Portal of Glory and Power in Angel Grove, so you could defend yourself against him.

{Angel Grove}

'It worked, our lord,' reports one of your little royal griffins. 'Our brothers from the distant mountains, whom you asked for help, have arrived and are at our disposal. They only want a little money to cover their journey, and then 
{they will help us in our great struggle!'}

map.[roe] - navrat klericky.sign.28.20.0:
Several bones and a crushed skull lie beneath the sign.
Burned into the sign are the words:

{CREMATORIUM}

